      <annotation addr="0800:29BB">[V] Return the input far pointer advanced by 0800h paragraphs (32 KiB), preserving its offset; tactical icon loading uses it to select packed graphics pages.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0DE8">[V] Read alternating 12-bit Westwood LZW codes from the compressed stream at 0800:0C97, return the code in AX and advance SI by one or two bytes according to the phase at 0800:0C99.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0ED9">[V] Read one of four packed 14-bit Westwood LZW code phases, return the code in AX and advance SI through the corresponding seven-byte group.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:0C33">[V] Select tactical-panel foreground color 03h for CGA and 05h for every other configured video adapter.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:146E">[V] Advance the 19x12 tactical cursor by one cell, wrapping X into the next row and the final row back to the origin.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:14E1">[V] Retreat the 19x12 tactical cursor by one cell, wrapping X into the previous row and the origin to the final cell.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:5755">[V] TranslateTacticalMouseInput_5755 consumes pending mouse buttons or movement and returns the equivalent tactical input code in AX. It maps clicks to Space/Escape, maps viewport-edge motion through DS:2EFE, and pans the overview map proportionally. The apparent DI output was incidental stack state.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:000B">[V] RunTacticalUnitCommandMenu_000B displays and runs the command menu for the supplied unit, including target, movement, formation, attack, and lance-order choices. Its only stack argument is unitIndex; the earlier DI:DS pseudo-argument was a corrupted segment inference.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:148A">[V] RunTacticalGameOptionsMenu_148A displays the in-battle options panel and dispatches its sound, music, game-speed, and related tactical settings. It has no stack arguments.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:2B0E">[V] ValidatePrimaryLanceLeader_2B0E returns nonzero in AX only while the supplied current leader remains the first deployed mobile unit of the primary four-unit lance; unit zero is invalidated when immobilized while another member remains mobile.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:079A">[V] Draw a 16x16 outline around the current viewport-relative tactical cursor cell, then XOR its stored color with 0Fh for the next blink phase.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:07C9">[V] Hide the mouse overlay, draw the four clipped sides of a 16x16 cell outline at the supplied pixel coordinates and color, then restore the overlay.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0926">[V] Draw a clipped Bresenham-style weapon trace from start to end. A nonzero dashedTrace plots every sixth pixel with a randomized initial phase.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0DDB">[V] Resolve spriteId through the four-byte pointer table at DS:83EE and draw it at viewport-relative pixels on the active framebuffer while tactical overview mode is inactive.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="375F:0100">[V] Poll bit 7 of the caller-selected Sound Blaster DSP write port until clear, then write the AH command/data byte.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="375F:015B">[V] Write packed AX low-byte register/high-byte value to the OPL register pair selected by DX, using the calibrated delays at 375F:0154/0156.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="375F:0163">[V] Complete an OPL register write: consume the caller-supplied register delay, write AH to DX+1, then consume the calibrated data delay.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0A7E">[V] Restart the Tandy three-voice round-robin scan from DS:68BE, reload the remaining-voice count from DS:68DB and tail-call the shared MIDI sequencer service.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0F55">[V] Wrap the MPU-401 transmit queue read cursor to zero, then enter 3621:0F57 to consume the transmitted byte.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0F57">[V] Store the caller-supplied BX cursor at DS:6D14 and decrement the queued-byte count at DS:6D16.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:0FDB">[V] Center a far string within the active tile window, add rowOffset to its top tile and draw it with the supplied foreground/background colors.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:5E6D">[P] Store one tactical slot's sprite state at DS:99AC+slotIndex; requested state 06h (unit not deployed) is normalized to sprite state 03h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0999">[V] Clear the 19x12 byte tactical-effect overlay map at physical aliases 4184:07D8 and DS:7978.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2D37">[V] Fill byteCount bytes at the supplied far destination with value; tactical-session setup uses it to zero the CB90h runtime allocation.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0C6F">[V] Draw a one-pixel border immediately outside the active text window's tile rectangle using the supplied color.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:1219">[V] Clear and rebuild the 19x12 tactical terrain-effect overlay from 90 six-byte DS:810C records, advancing each visible effect through three animation variants unless paused.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:1D06">[P] Advance optional terrain effects, then refresh the ordinary tactical viewport or overview presentation and restore its cursor/status overlays.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:1D61">[V] Calculate one unit's remaining durability, format friendly units as an exact percentage and opposing units in 10-percent steps, then append the percent suffix.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:09BB">[V] Composite two indexed 16x16 tactical sprites from one far sprite page directly into the interleaved CGA framebuffer.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0A2E">[V] Draw one 16x16 sprite from the CGA-specific 0100h..01FFh tactical sprite bank directly into B800h memory.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:116F">[V] Draw one indexed 16x16 tactical tile through the active CGA, Tandy, EGA or VGA framebuffer path.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2483">[V] Composite two indexed 16x16 tactical sprites at one destination through the active adapter-specific framebuffer path.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:264B">[V] Register-call EGA compositor inner step: select one plane, combine one byte from each sprite using the supplied mask and write two destination bytes.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:1CBD">[V] Dispatch CGA sprite IDs 0100h..01FFh to the packed high-bank renderer and every other adapter/ID combination to the general tactical-tile renderer.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:14DF">[P] Redraw and cache the primary unit-status row outline when either its row index or blink color changes.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:1544">[P] Redraw and cache the secondary unit-command row outline when either its row index or display color changes.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:099E">[V] Silence CX Tandy PSG voices beginning at DS:BX, update each cached attenuation latch and tail-call the base MIDI-driver deactivation hook.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0A6B">[V] Not a procedure: 0A6Bh is the C0h immediate port operand of the OUT instruction beginning at 0A6Ah. Suppress this overlapping Reko entry.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0BEE">[V] Program one five-byte OPL operator patch from DS:DI using AL as the base operator register and CL bits 30h to select the optional total-level write; return the original operator index in AL.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0BFF">[V] Shared OPL operator-programming tail: write packed AX, then the 60h, 80h and E0h groups from DS:DI and return the original operator index in AL. Leave this as an inferred shared tail: a user C signature cannot describe its nonstandard clobber set and destabilizes structure analysis.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0BFC">[V] Not a procedure: 0BFCh is the 30h immediate operand of TEST CL,30h beginning at 0BFAh. The earlier ProgramAdLibOperatorPair label was an overlapping-decode artifact.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:130C">[V] Clear the three damaged-weapon range flags at DS:99C2 and scan all eight equipment-location arrays in the selected 96h-byte persistent unit record.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:140F">[V] Scan one equipment-location array; for each damaged one-based weapon ID, set its long-, medium-, or close-range flag at DS:99C2..99C4.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:2AA6">[P] Trace line of sight from one of four enabled DS:865B/865F tactical reference points to the selected live unit's DS:8562/857B map coordinates.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="30F1:0A3F">[V] Copy one three-byte DS:5928 scenario-allegiance row across the first three four-unit persistent-roster groups, storing each value in unit field +94h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:1014">[V] Prepare the selected unit's displayed combat ratings. Friendly and detected enemies use actual damage; an undetected enemy uses an undamaged estimate. Lance leaders produce a four-unit average. Return nonzero while enemy damage must remain concealed.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:10F4">[V] Recalculate and average all six combat-rating words for the deployed units in the leader's four-slot lance, using actual or undamaged-estimate records as requested.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:11D2">[V] Build the 96h-byte rating scratch record at DS:84C7 from maximum armor, widened weapon-family counts and equipment IDs with their damage bits removed, concealing exact enemy damage.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:04B5">[V] Render the shared DS:38BE formatted-text line-break command used between rows in the tactical command and game-options panels.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:04C2">[V] Draw the complete tactical detail/control panel for one persistent unit: visibility-sensitive identity and condition, combat ratings, durability, movement, equipment upgrades, and enemy assessment text.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0CA6">[V] Not a procedure entry: this is the second PUSH in the shared AdLib voice-on implementation. Entering here leaves its two later POP instructions unbalanced.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0CB5">[V] Not a procedure entry: fall-through patch-loading block inside the AdLib voice-on implementation, reached only with BX/AX already saved at 0CA5/0CA6.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0CDE">[V] Not a procedure entry: shared pitch/key-on tail inside the AdLib voice-on implementation, reached with its caller-owned saved registers already on the stack.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0328">[V] Draw one rebuilt 19x12 viewport cell, composing the unit sprite, temporary terrain-effect sprite and base terrain tile as required.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0AA4">[V] Append one 0Eh-byte tactical projectile record for a missile-class weapon, including attacker/target, hit state, octant sprite, source coordinates and destination coordinates.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:1586">[V] Resolve the deployed friendly or visible enemy unit under the tactical cursor, update DS:03DC, and resynchronize the cursor and cached viewport-relative coordinates to that unit.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:1732">[V] Apply one cardinal or diagonal input code to the tactical cursor, scrolling the 19x12 viewport at its edges and clearing the selected-unit index after movement.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:18C9">[V] Move a weapon-trace target endpoint eight pixels away from the target center along the source-to-target octant, interpolating the other coordinate so the line terminates at the unit sprite edge.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:1A83">[P] Advance scenario-driven random area impacts, move an active impact source toward its destination, and occasionally seed a new map-edge visual effect.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:410C">[P] Map a friendly unit or four-unit lance leader to tactical status slot 0-6; opposing units map to slot 7 and unrepresented friendly followers return FFFFh.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:49CC">[V] Keep the tactical cursor locked to DS:03DC's selected unit, pan and clamp the viewport to follow it, and refresh the cursor's viewport-relative coordinates.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:51C0">[P] Rebuild the seven tactical status-slot sprite states from each friendly unit's deployment, visibility and half-durability state while preserving the current lance-panel mode.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:52F2">[V] Advance the tactical campaign clock by two minutes, carrying at 60 minutes and 60 hours and wrapping the day byte at 24, then redraw the clock.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:5577">[P] Build the scenario-specific terrain-damage capability map at DS:A865 from the selected terrain-effect mode, configured type ranges and the loaded 300h-byte terrain capability table.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:5D8A">[P] Enable unit field +8Ch for friendly units carrying qualifying missile ammunition when either of the two scenario missile-upgrade flags is active.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:2224">[P] Draw the four-pixel lance-formation marker selected by the low seven bits of formationCode at the requested active-window tile column.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:25F0">[V] Format map coordinates into DS:B67E as a five-by-five sector letter A-Y followed by two decimal within-sector digits and a NUL terminator.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:2A8A">[V] Temporarily move the tactical cursor across a leader's deployed followers and draw an outline around each follower currently visible in the 19x12 viewport.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:1185">[V] Encode display-backing rows. CGA copies alternating packed bytes, Tandy copies packed words, and EGA emits sparse pixel-mask/color pairs with 80h group, 40h row and 20h image terminator bits.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:129E">[V] Register helper: return the original high nibble in DL and shift BX left four bits for the next packed-pixel extraction.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0E19">[P] Resolve the selected or contacted tactical unit, draw its status fields in UI window 6, and clear stale selection state when no valid unit remains.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:16E8">[V] Advance four-word impact-sprite records at DS:B2F4 and compact the queue when an animation reaches its terminal sprite.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:17DE">[V] Advance 0Eh-byte projectile records at DS:A9DD toward their target cells; apply weapon damage, queue the arrival impact and compact completed records.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:1AE3">[P] Advance four-word map-edge effect records at DS:A800, emit occasional secondary impact visuals and compact records that leave the tactical map.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="34A7:0014">[V] Install the Borland default DOS critical-error callback at CS:0006.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="34A7:0059">[V] Save the supplied far callback at DS:B888/B88A and install the resident CS:0021 dispatcher as DOS INT 24h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="39E5:0043">[V] Build and far-call a stack-resident INT opcode thunk, transfer the supplied register block through it, capture FLAGS and output registers, and translate carry-set DOS errors.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="39F3:0000">[V] Capture ES, CS, SS and DS into the four-word segment-state block used by the run-time interrupt bridge.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="39F8:0000">[V] Borland-compatible stateful far-string tokenizer: skip leading delimiters, NUL-terminate the next token and retain DS:B88E/B890 as the continuation cursor.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0959">[V] Install the far pointer 0800:01C9 to the damaged-terrain sprite lookup table in the graphics runtime slot at 4184:08D3.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:05D3">[V] BuildTacticalTerrainCellMaps_05D3 clears the 19x12 sprite layer, copies the visible terrain IDs into the adjacent terrain layer, and replaces damaged cells through the packed two-bit damage map and the 0800:01C9 sprite lookup table.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:01C9">[V] DamagedTerrainSpriteLookup_01C9 contains three 100h-byte mappings, indexed by damage state 1-3 and the original terrain type.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="4184:0901">[V] TacticalMapRowWidth_0901 is the graphics runtime's terrain-map row width (60h in the load image), used by viewport map construction and line-of-sight traversal.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0650">[V] RebuildTacticalViewport_0650 rebuilds the two 19x12 cell maps for DS:84A0/83DA, composes unit and effect sprites, draws all 228 cells, then refreshes tactical indicators.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:0670">[V] Build the base terrain and empty sprite layers from TerrainTypeMap_83EA into TacticalCellSpriteMap_99BC and the immediately adjacent TacticalCellTerrainMap_8823.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:0000">[V] Own the complete tactical session: allocate and partition CB90h bytes of map state, capture 29 UI backing buffers, load scenario assets, initialize units and rendering, run the interaction loop, then release every session allocation. Reko 0.12.4 is deliberately prevented from regenerating this verified routine because its high-level expression builder loses the valid 1A1F:02DC basic block after SSA conversion; retain the last good output in reko.old and the maintained annotation C.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:0351">[P] Advance and redraw one tactical frame. The first argument is the normalized input/action value; the second requests initial per-unit setup when nonzero.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:0613">[P] Run the tactical interaction loop until the scenario reaches its exit condition.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:1132">[P] Initialize per-unit tactical runtime arrays from the persistent 96h-byte roster records before the first rendered frame.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:1C48">[P] Load the map, icon set, SCENE data, roster placement, and scenario-specific tactical state selected by the ASCII scenario code. Reko 0.12.4 is deliberately prevented from redecompiling this address because its SSA transformer recurses without bound while resolving BX and then crashes the high-level region builder; retain the last good output in reko.old and the maintained annotation C.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:159F">[P] Redraw the ordinary tactical viewport when the overview is inactive, including deployed-unit sprites and overlays.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="31FB:00B3">[V] Deduplicate the 16 digital weapon-effect records by resource index, assign packed offsets and lengths, allocate one sample bank, and load each distinct resource exactly once.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="31FB:12A7">[V] Release the packed digital weapon-effect sample bank rooted at DS:B629:B62B.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:1CCC">[V] For one unit, scan the opposing twelve deployed records for line of sight, set DS:8667, latch first contact at DS:87ED, and queue the first-contact narration transition.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:11F7">[P] Focus the tactical view on one unit: smoothly center the 19x12 viewport when the unit is off-screen, update cursor-relative and selected-unit state, and move the mouse cursor to the resulting cell.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:1E43">[V] For one contacted unit, scan the opposing twelve deployed records; compare tactical distance against the 14h/0Ah/00h DS:03E7 threshold indexed by the opponent's zero/one/two sensor hits, then set DS:8680 and DS:8806 on the first strict-less-than match.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:08AF">[V] Recalculate combat ratings for all 24 deployed unit records, forwarding rebuildWeaponCounts and advancing recovery, then run tactical target selection.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:08FA">[V] Select or retain each deployed unit's tactical target, combine allied durability/firepower against a shared target, and map the comparison mask through DS:08C6 into DS:AED6.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:08C6">[V] TacticalEngagementModeLookup_08C6 is a 256-byte comparison-mask table returning close 01h, medium 02h, long 03h, or withdraw 04h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:A7F3">[V] UnitLastNarratedTarget_A7F3 contains 24 target bytes used to suppress repeated category-0Ah withdrawal narration.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:AED6">[V] UnitPreferredEngagementMode_AED6 contains 24 movement policies: none 00h, close 01h, medium 02h, long 03h, withdraw 04h, position 05h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:03EA">[V] Try neighboring cells in rotating direction order, enforce terrain/class/collision rules, advance route and exit state, then update position, terrain, facing, sprite, heat, and terrain damage.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:0F1F">[V] Derive movement eligibility from walk movement, heat, terrain and jump state; choose route, target, withdrawal, or formation coordinates; face the target and attempt one map step.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8827">[V] UnitJumpingState_8827 contains 24 active-jump flags controlling movement cadence, sprite animation, heat, and attack modifiers.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:9993">[V] UnitTerrainType_9993 contains the current terrain ID beneath each tactical unit.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:99C7">[V] UnitMovementHeatExponent_99C7 contains 24 SCENE-controlled movement modes: zero disables movement, 02h grants 1.5x base movement, and nonzero values select ground-movement heat.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:AE3D">[V] UnitJumpMovementRemaining_AE3D contains 24 counters initialized from unit-record jump movement +03h and decremented while jumping.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:14A4">[V] Execute one unit's weapon AI: enforce shutdown and experience-indexed heat limits, classify distance/heat/arc, select the first available weapon from DS:0F46/0F66/0FA6 priority data, resolve the attack, and return whether it occurred.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:1B33">[V] Select a legal lance formation from deployed member count, scenario profile DS:8650, leader experience, comparative strength, and optional random selection through DS:2F72/2F7E/2F8A.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:23AC">[V] Convert map X/Y to the packed two-bit terrain-damage field and begin damage only while that field is zero.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:23F8">[V] Set ordinary terrain to damage state one immediately, or append a packed-byte/subcell pair for the three special destructible terrain types to the staged queue at DS:B28E.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8106">[V] TerrainDamageQueueWordCount_8106 is the used-word count for paired entries in the 32h-word DS:B28E queue.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8650">[P] LanceFormationProfile_8650 contains six scenario-supplied profile bytes used to choose formation tables and deterministic leader formations.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B28E">[V] TerrainDamageQueue_B28E contains up to 25 packed-byte/subcell pairs advanced by 2007:042A.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:03E0">[V] WeaponAIHeatLimitByExperience_03E0 is the byte table 14h,10h,0Dh,0Ah,08h; weapon AI indexes experience+1 normally or experience while DS:890C is active.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2208:043C">[V] Toggle DS:890C for the selected unit. The command panel labels the states Close Assault/Cease Assault for infantry damage model 03h, otherwise Overburn: Off/Overburn: On.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:41DF">[V] Two far-string pointers indexed by DS:890C: Close Assault and Cease Assault.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:420D">[V] Two far-string pointers indexed by DS:890C: Overburn: Off and Overburn: On.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:890C">[V] UnitOverburnOrCloseAssaultEnabled_890C contains 24 Boolean bytes. It selects infantry close assault or non-infantry overburn, propagates with lance orders, and is cleared by heat shutdown.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:0F46">[V] WeaponPriorityListCounts_0F46 contains 16 word counts for the far priority lists selected by DS:0FA6.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:0F66">[V] WeaponPriorityListPointers_0F66 contains 16 far pointers to mask-and-weapon-choice lists.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:0FA6">[V] WeaponPriorityProfileByRangeHeat_0FA6 maps the fixed distance bits 10h/20h/40h and heat-category bits 01h/02h/04h/08h to a priority-list index.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:256B">[V] Run the 2d6 heat-shutdown check for one unit using whole heat at record +87h, capped at 30; failure clears DS:890C[unit] and sets DS:A84A[unit].</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8680">[P] UnitEnemyInProximityRange_8680 contains 24 flags set by 2208:1E43 after first contact and a DS:03E7 threshold match.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:87ED">[V] UnitEnemyContactEstablished_87ED contains 24 latches set on first line of sight to any deployed opponent.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8806">[V] UnitEnemyEngagementActive_8806 contains 24 flags set alongside DS:8680 by 2208:1E43.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:88A4">[V] UnitTacticalTarget_88A4 contains selected target unit indices, 18h for the ground-coordinate target, or FFh for none; target selection, movement, weapon AI, narration, and lance recovery consume it.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:A84A">[V] UnitShutdownState_A84A contains 24 heat-shutdown flags; 2D1B:256B sets them and movement/weapon AI skip affected units.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:23F0">[V] Save the prior BIOS INT 1Ch callback and install GameClockInt1CHandler_2440.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:241E">[V] Restore the prior BIOS INT 1Ch callback during game shutdown.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2440">[V] BIOS user-timer callback at approximately 18.2065 Hz: decrement DS:5923 and DS:5925, increment the two 32-bit counters at DS:591B and DS:591F, then chain the saved handler.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:17DA">[V] TacticalUpdateDelayReloadTicks_17DA: speed keys 1 through 8 select 50h,32h,23h,19h,0Fh,09h,05h,02h BIOS ticks.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:591B">[V] GameTimerTicks_591B is a free-running 32-bit BIOS INT 1Ch tick count.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:591F">[V] GameAnimationTicks_591F is a second free-running 32-bit INT 1Ch tick count; low-word bit 10h drives the campaign-clock separator blink.</annotation>
