      <annotation addr="35CA:0009">[V] ToggleActiveUiRegionHighlight_0009 XORs the rectangle cached at DS:B652-B65A; a second call restores the underlying pixels.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B6D0">[V] ActiveUiRegionIndex_B6D0: selects a 10h-byte record from UiRegionTable_07AA.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:058E">AmmoCapacityMultiplierTable_058E: 14 word entries multiplied by per-unit weapon counts to rebuild ammunition values in ResetLiveUnitState_0878.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:197B">[P] SavedScenarioUnitMapX_197B: 24 one-byte per-unit coordinates copied from DS:8562 before scenario-specific roster construction and serialized in each save slot. X/Y ordering awaits a movement trace.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:1993">[P] SavedScenarioUnitMapY_1993: 24 one-byte per-unit coordinates copied from DS:857B before scenario-specific roster construction and serialized in each save slot. X/Y ordering awaits a movement trace.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:1956">[V] SaveCampaignSnapshot_1956: 221h-byte campaign-state block assembled before save and unpacked after load. Each file slot appends 24 complete 96h-byte live-unit records.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:24D6">[P] CampaignStageIndex_24D6: winning saves progress from 0001h at Scenario 2 through 0014h at Scenario 26 and 0015h at Pacifica training.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:24D8">[H] ScenarioVariantIndex_24D8: supplied training checkpoints use variant IDs 0,2,4,1,3,5.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:24DA">[P] CampaignPhase_24DA: advances from 1 through 8 across supplied campaign checkpoints.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:24DC">[H] TrainingSequenceFlag_24DC: set for supplied training checkpoints T1-T5.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:24DF">[P] CampaignFlags_24DF: serialized bitfield; bit 0 influences live-unit reset in the SCENEN roster recipe.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:1CCA">[V/P] UnitLanceAssignmentTable_1CCA: 13 serialized 0Ah-byte roster UI records. +00/+02/+04 hold probable left/top/width geometry, +06 style, +07 persistent-roster slot, +08 live-unit slot, and +09 pilot ID. DrawUnitRosterScreen_26EE verifies +08/+09.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:1D4C">[P] PilotRosterTable_1D4C: 37 four-byte entries. The entry index is stored as unit pilot ID +92h; entry +01 supplies pilot experience +93h, entry +02 supplies gunnery target +8Ah, and entry +03 is availability.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:1D4F">[P] PilotAvailabilityTable_1D4F: 37 four-byte entries indexed by unit field +92h. First byte 01h means its populated persistent unit has active deployment state, FFh means that unit is inactive, and 00h is default/unestablished. Save/load preserves only this first byte.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:855F">ScenarioClockSnapshot_855F: three-byte snapshot copied from CampaignClock_8337 before scenario roster preparation and included in save/load state.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8562">[V] ScenarioUnitMapX_8562: 24 one-byte live-unit map X coordinates, copied to DS:197B and consumed by line-of-sight, weapon-trace, and damage-direction routines.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:857B">[V] ScenarioUnitMapY_857B: 24 one-byte live-unit map Y coordinates, copied to DS:1993 and consumed by line-of-sight, weapon-trace, and damage-direction routines.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:85B0">EmptyUnitRecord_85B0: blank 96h-byte unit record copied over unused or vacated roster slots.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:86C1">[P] UnitMovementRoutes_86C1: 24 records of 0Bh bytes containing route index, active X/Y, four X waypoints, and four Y waypoints. SCENE F9h initializes them and AdvanceUnitSceneRoute_469C consumes them.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8B81">PersistentUnitRoster_8B81: 24 contiguous 96h-byte unit records spanning DS:8B81-9990.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:99E0">LiveScenarioUnits_99E0: 24 contiguous 96h-byte tactical unit records spanning DS:99E0-A7EF.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B581">[V] ScenarioFileSuffix_B581: ASCII 31h-39h and 41h-54h select SCENE1.DAT-SCENET.DAT and dispatch their roster recipes.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:10B0">[P] CachedFileDescriptorTable_10B0: 12h-byte records containing a far filename pointer, 32-bit file length, optional far cached-data pointer, flags/ID, and 32-bit current position.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B63A">[P] OpenStreamHandleTable_B63A: ten word entries; 7FFFh marks a free slot and bit 15 selects a memory-backed cached stream instead of a DOS handle.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B652">[V] ActiveUiHighlightXorColor_B652 through ActiveUiHighlightTop_B65A cache the XOR color, pixel height, pixel width, left, and top of the most recent UI selection highlight.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B66A">[V] SavedUiRegionSelectionRows_B66A is a byte array populated before grouped selection and copied back into DS:07B2 records when the user cancels.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="30B2:00DF">Decode a PC-speaker music stream: note/duration pairs, loop controls CDh/CEh and D1h/D2h, duration-scale controls E2h/E8h/E9h, E6h word frequency in Hz plus duration, and terminator FFh. E8h wraps byte subtraction; E9h clamps to FFh only on x86 signed overflow (JNO), not unsigned carry. All 16 embedded streams decode exactly; 319 encoded instructions expand to 460 PIT/rest events over 2088 duration ticks.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="30B2:0298">SilencePCSpeaker_0298 clears the speaker-enable and PIT-channel-2 gate bits at port 61h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:4611">Display the invalid-save-version dialog used by the save-file validation path. This routine does not load the game state.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:24DF">Show the three-entry main menu using MenuOptionTextTable_25E5: New Game, Load Game, and Game Options.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:25F5">V: Lay out the three main-menu labels supplied as a far-pointer table, repeat selection while Escape is returned, and return the selected UI-region action.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:35AA">V: Prepare the mission-date background. Modes 0-1 select screen resources 16h-17h; modes 2-4 load graphics resource 18h and capture sprite-layout entry 09h or 0Ah.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:365C">V: Draw the framed mission-map header and DS:2489 heading using the eight-pixel font.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:376C">V: Format and animate an indexed campaign date using DS:2459, 273F, 274B, and 2763; optionally blink the indexed map rectangle at DS:271C-2738.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:3AE4">V/P: Display an indexed five-byte mission follow-up record from DS:2B54; +00h is the far text pointer and +04h selects its text-window placement.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:4155">V: Capture an indexed graphics-resource rectangle using the four geometry tables at DS:2783-27CB.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2007:132C">V: Convert a text-cell position through the active text-window origin and font metrics, then draw a raised beveled menu button of the supplied pixel width.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2507:0501">V: Render six BattleTech unit-class rows plus Cancel from UnitClassMenuTextTable_32F8, then return the selected MECHTYPE.DAT type ID through SelectUnitTypeFromList_0625 or FFFFh for Cancel.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2507:0625">V: Render an FFh-terminated MECHTYPE.DAT unit-type ID list through UnitNameTable_3D2E, append Cancel, and return the chosen type ID or FFFFh. For Friendly allegiance, the DS:32D7 Omni list suppresses its final Elementals ID before appending Cancel.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:32D7">V: OmniUnitTypeIdList_32D7 contains Puma, Black Hawk, Mad Cat, Elementals, FFh. SelectUnitTypeFromList_0625 suppresses Elementals unless ActiveUnitAllegiance_30CA is Enemy.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:32DC">V: UnitTypeListByClass_32DC contains six far pointers to the FFh-terminated Light, Medium, Heavy, Assault, Enhanced, and Omni unit-type ID lists.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2507:0A20">V: Draw the active Friendly/Enemy heading from DS:30CB; the sole stack argument indexes the panel text-color byte at DS:34C2.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2507:483A">Draw the detailed unit-status screen. This routine indexes UnitNameTable_3D2E and WeaponDefinitionTable_0435 and directly renders ARMOR:, HEAT:, and EXIT.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2507:60D2">V: Draw LNG, MED, CLS, and SPD from UnitStatAbbreviationTable_30F2, beginning at the supplied Y coordinate and advancing seven pixels per label.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2507:6111">V: Draw EXP and GUN from the tail of UnitStatAbbreviationTable_30F2, beginning at the supplied Y coordinate and advancing nine pixels per label. The entry includes PUSH BP at 6111h; call sites encode 2507:6111.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2507:623D">V: Free an inclusive range in the far graphics-backing-buffer pointer table beginning at DS:83EE.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B2D:0077">CountOrRemoveUnitHeatSinks_0077 starts with the unit record's +54h engine heat-sink capacity, counts equipment ID 18h in slots +55h through +83h, optionally clears installed heat sinks, and returns the total in AX.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B2D:0191">CalculateUnitWeaponHeatScale_0191 returns the 00h..05h heat-display index in AX. It adds installed weapon heat and the movement baseline, subtracts CountOrRemoveUnitHeatSinks_0077, clamps to 00h..1Eh, divides by four, and caps the result at 05h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:01AB">V: FindUnitWeaponByOrdinal_01AB(unitRecord, weaponOccurrence, removeWeapon); scans the eight location-specific equipment groups for one-based weapon IDs 01h..17h. On removal, it clears the slot and clears the ammunition-family count and current ammunition when no weapon of that exact type remains.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:0422">V: Convert a close-, medium-, or long-range combat rating to a descriptor index by dividing nonzero values by nine and capping at five; zero selects index six (None). Draw the selected far string from DS:40CF at the supplied pixel coordinates and colors.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2B34:0469">CountUnitWeaponsByType_0469(const unsigned char far *unitRecord) rebuilds the 23-word table at DS:88BF by scanning the contiguous equipment slots at unit-record offsets +55h through +83h. Its single far-pointer argument and void return are verified from the assembly.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:40CF">V: CombatRatingDescriptionTable_40CF; seven far pointers to Light, Moderate, Heavy, Brutal, Devastating, Incredible, and None.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B015">V: SelectedUnitCloseRangeRating_B015; +04h field of scratch derived-combat record 18h at DS:B011.</annotation>
