      <annotation addr="3A6A:B019">V: SelectedUnitLongRangeRating_B019; +08h field of scratch derived-combat record 18h at DS:B011.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:0005">V: RecalculateUnitCombatRatings_0005; optionally rebuilds and caches 23 installed weapon counts, advances DS:8929 recovery counters, excludes weapons lacking ammunition, constructs each 23-bit DS:A971 availability mask, and writes movement, durability, close/medium/long firepower, and sensor damage to the 0Ch-byte DS:AEF1 record.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8596">V: UnitBelowHalfDurability_8596; 24 one-byte flags latched TRUE when combat-rating refresh finds current armor or structure below half maximum.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B04F">V: UnitCachedWeaponCounts_B04F; 24 by 23 byte low-count cache restored into the DS:88BF word table when combat ratings are refreshed without rescanning equipment.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:03DC">V: TacticalSelectedUnitIndex_03DC; current focused tactical unit or FFFFh. Selection and camera paths write it; withdrawal and destruction clear it.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:03DE">P: EnemyCycleUnitIndex_03DE; remembered opposing-unit slot for the visible-enemy cycle command, copied into DS:03DC when selected and cleared when that unit leaves play.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:885B">V: UnitDestructionMarkers_885B; 24 three-byte records of map X, map Y, and destruction sprite code. DCh marks friendly destruction and DDh opposing destruction; the tactical renderer draws sprite 0100h plus the code.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:072C">V: CalculateSelectedWeaponRating_072C; return a 32-bit DX:AX weighted sum for the selected bits of a 23-bit weapon mask. Counts are words at DS:88BF and weights are bytes at 4184:08BC.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:3498">V: ConvertPackedPixelsToEGAPlanar_3498; transpose eight packed 4-bit pixels at a time into EGA plane bytes 0, 1, 2, and 3. The apparent DH:DL register inputs are fully shifted out before each store and are not semantic arguments.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:32ED">V: RepackCgaAlternateScanlines_32ED copies 250 40h-byte rows backwards from a 40h-stride source layout into an 80h-stride CGA alternate-scanline layout.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:3327">V: FillTandyPackedRectangle_3327 fills an inclusive row count in four interleaved 2000h-byte Tandy video banks; each output byte repeats the four-bit color in both pixel nibbles.</annotation>
