      <annotation addr="0800:35D8">V: ConvertCgaPackedPixelsAndBuildMask_35D8 converts 3E80h packed pixel pairs in place through alternating CGA phase tables and replaces the second byte of each pair with a four-pixel transparency mask.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:3571">V: ConvertCgaPackedPixels_3571 consumes two packed source bytes per output byte, alternates the 100h-byte CGA phase lookup tables after the caller-supplied run length, and has no semantic return value.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:4D81">V: DOS_SelectDefaultDrive is INT 21h/AH=0Eh; its byte argument is the zero-based drive number.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:4D98">V: BIOS_SelectCgaPalette is INT 10h/AH=0Bh with BH=01h and the palette selector in BL.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:34E3">V: ShiftPackedPixelsIntoEGAPlanes_34E3; internal carry-chain helper that shifts one packed pixel nibble into the four EGA plane accumulators. Reko 0.12.4 miscounts the near RET as a four-byte return, so the complete signature is retained with decompilation disabled.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:540B">V: CompareNormalizedFarPointers; normalize two real-mode far pointers to offsets 0..0Fh, compare segment then offset, and return the normalized left pointer through DX:AX.</annotation>
	  <annotation addr="0800:53B0">V: AddSignedOffsetToFarPointer; add signed CX:BX to DX:AX and return a normalized real-mode pointer in DX:AX with offset 0000h..000Fh.</annotation>
	  <annotation addr="38FE:0002">V: ResizeProgramBreak_0002(newBreak); resize the owning DOS memory block in 1 KiB increments, update the exact current break, and tighten the maximum break after DOS reports an insufficient block.</annotation>
	  <annotation addr="38FE:0092">V: SetProgramBreak(newBreak); Borland brk-style checked setter returning 0000h on success or FFFFh on failure.</annotation>
