      <annotation addr="3A6A:1038">V: HitLocationTables_1038; five 18h-byte tables containing 11 word results for 2d6 rolls 2..12 plus zero padding. Tables 0..3 are rear, right side, front, and left side; table 4 is the fixed infantry target.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:3CFE">V: HitLocationTableByFacing_3CFE; 16 word selectors with values 0..3, indexed by target facing plus relative attack direction.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:3D0D">P: ImprovedMissileDamageBonusTable_3D0D; byte table indexed by weapon index 10h-16h when the attacking unit's class-dependent missile-upgrade byte +8Ch is nonzero.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="2D1B:1EC5">P: UnitRecord +8Ch is missileUpgradeState. Normal units add ImprovedMissileDamageBonusTable_3D0D to missile damage; infantry use the same byte for the inferno heat-only attack path.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:A9D9">V: SceneInstructionOffset_A9D9; offset half of the far bytecode cursor consumed and advanced by ExecuteSceneInstructions_2A4E.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:A9DB">V: SceneInstructionSegment_A9DB; segment half of the far bytecode cursor.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:A862">[V] SceneInstructionBaseOffset_A862: file offset 0128h for SCENE1, derived from the first SCENE data offset plus its reserved word. Script branch words are absolute offsets relative to this base.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:8927">[V] NarrationMessageCategory_8927: values 00h-0Ah select one of 11 generic messages inside a six-speaker bank. SCENE DCh-E1h stores 10h-0Bh respectively to select the six trailing event strings.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:B2F2">[P] ActiveNarrationSubject_B2F2: combat narration stores a unit index; SCENE DCh-E1h stores the instruction byte operand. Voice/sound selection compares 01h-04h, supporting a speaker role, but exact identities remain unassigned.</annotation>
	  <annotation addr="3A6A:8104">V: TacticalOverviewActive_8104; nonzero selects tactical-overview rendering and incidentally suppresses the ordinary campaign clock. ExitTacticalOverview_0401 clears it.</annotation>
	  <annotation addr="3A6A:8374">V: TacticalOverviewMarkerX_8374; 24 cached unit-marker X coordinates, with FFh meaning absent.</annotation>
