      <annotation addr="3621:007E">V: SendMIDIAllNotesOff_007E emits MIDI control-change 7Bh with value zero on all 16 channels.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:00AA">V: ReadMIDIVariableLengthQuantity_00AA consumes a MIDI variable-length quantity from ES:SI, returns the decoded value in AX, and advances SI.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:00C1">V: StartMIDISequence_00C1 validates a format-zero, one-track, 96-division MThd/MTrk stream, reads its initial delta time, and installs the track cursor and playback flags.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0193">V: PauseMIDISequence_0193 sets playback flag 04h and silences every channel while retaining the current stream cursor.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:01B1">V: ResumeMIDISequence_01B1 clears playback flag 04h when an active sequence is paused.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:01CC">V: StopMIDISequence_01CC clears the active playback flags and sends all-notes-off.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:004B">V: ConfigureMIDITempo_004B stores BPM at DS:624A, atomically sets DS:624E to ticks-per-quarter-note times BPM, and clears the timing remainder. FF 51 calls it with the fixed 60h PPQN stream division.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0063">V: ConfigureMIDITimeSignature_0063 converts FF 58 numerator, denominator, and derived beats-per-measure into the DS:6252 tick-to-beat and DS:6254 beat-to-measure divisors.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:01E8">V: ServiceMIDISequenceTick_01E8 advances fixed-point MIDI time, consumes every due event, implements running status and pause suppression, dispatches channel/system messages through the in-function targets listed at DS:6266/6274, and interprets FF 01 channel-map, FF 2F end-track, FF 51 tempo, and FF 58 time-signature events. DS is restored to 3A6Ah by the IRQ caller.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0388">V: DivideUnsigned32_0388 is a hand-written unsigned 32-bit restoring divide returning the quotient in DX:AX. The tempo path uses it for 60,000,000 divided by microseconds per quarter note.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:03EE">V: DispatchMIDIByte_03EE feeds one status or data byte through the active driver filter and MIDI message parser.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0514">P: PrepareMIDIDriver_0514 invokes callback +04h in the selected DS-resident driver descriptor. The exact vendor terminology for this stage remains unknown.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:051E">V: ActivateMIDIDriver_051E takes the descriptor offset omitted by the prior decompile, shuts down the previous driver, activates the selected driver, copies its voice count, and resets playback state.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0542">V: DeactivateMIDIDriver_0542 invokes the active descriptor's +08h shutdown callback and restores the null descriptor at DS:6766.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0550">P: MIDIDriverHandlesByte_0550 passes one MIDI byte to callback +0Ah and returns its AX result. The exact meaning is probably handled/filtered but needs a driver-specific trace.</annotation>
