      <annotation addr="3621:0832">V: ResetMIDIPlaybackState_0832 clears channel/voice state, rebuilds the voice-node list for the active driver's voice count, and invokes callback +10h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:08A1">V: ServiceActiveMIDIDriver_08A1 tail-calls the active driver descriptor's interrupt-time callback at +14h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0931">V: PC-speaker MIDI service round-robins 20h-byte voice records and reprograms PIT channel 2 only when the selected voice divisor changes.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0A5C">V: Tandy MIDI service writes a frequency word and attenuation latch for one hardware voice per tick, then advances the three-voice round-robin cursor.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0B96">V: IBM PS/1 MIDI service mirrors the Tandy three-voice scheduler through audio port 0205h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:67A6">V: PC-speaker MIDI voice-record base, voice count, current PIT divisor, service cursor, remaining count, and divisor table occupy 67A6h-6881h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:68D8">V: Tandy MIDI round-robin cursor/count state at 68D8h-68DBh followed by its note-frequency word table at 68DCh.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:69A4">V: IBM PS/1 MIDI round-robin cursor/count state at 69A4h-69A7h followed by its note-frequency word table at 69A8h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0C2B">V: AdLib MIDI probe uses the canonical OPL2 timer-1 status transition and derives the two port-I/O delay counts at DS:6A6E/6A70.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0DEB">V: Expands an 11-byte packed instrument definition into the driver's 0Ch-byte OPL operator patch format using SI as source and DI as destination.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0EF4">V: Roland byte filter remaps channel-status bytes through DS:6728 and enqueues every byte in the 100h-byte MPU-401 transmit ring.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0F33">V: Roland service sends at most one queued byte to MPU-401 data port 0330h when status bit 40h reports output ready.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3621:0F60">V: MPU-401 IRQ handler drains one input byte from port 0330h and acknowledges the master PIC.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="21E7:0044">V: ReadResourceFileSpan_0044 opens the selected resource, seeks to the supplied 32-bit offset, reads byteCount bytes to a far destination, and closes the handle.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="21E7:000C">V: ReadWholeResourceFile_000C opens a resource, reads the requested 16-bit byte count to a far destination, closes it, and returns the number of bytes read.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="21E7:008E">V: LoadAndDecodePackedResource_008E consumes the outer 16-bit stored-length word, reads that many bytes into a paragraph-aligned workspace, and dispatches the embedded Westwood compression header.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="21E7:00F4">V: DecodeWestwoodPackedResource_00F4 dispatches compression types 0 raw copy, 1 LZW-12, 2 LZW-14, and 3 byte RLE; types 1 and 2 use 3C00h and BD00h dictionary workspaces.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0C34">V: CopyUncompressedFarBlock_0C34 copies the 32-bit byte count from one normalized far buffer to another, rebasing both pointers across segment boundaries.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0D1A">V: DecodeWestwoodLzw12_0D1A expands compression type 1. The block stores its uncompressed byte count at +02h and optional-header size at +06h; packed codes start at +08h plus that size. Two 12-bit codes occupy three bytes. The 3C00h-byte dictionary has 0F00h four-byte entries containing a word prefix and byte suffix.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:0E16">V: DecodeWestwoodLzw14_0E16 expands compression type 2 from the same +02h/+06h block header. Four 14-bit codes occupy seven bytes. The BD00h-byte dictionary stores 3F00h prefix words at 0000h and their suffix bytes at 7E00h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2683">V: CopyBufferToVideoRegion_2683 restores a captured rectangle. Coordinates are 8-pixel columns/rows; height becomes scanlines. CGA uses two interleaved banks, Tandy four, EGA restores four plane bytes per screen byte, and VGA is linear 320-byte scanlines.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2835">V: CopyVideoRegionToBuffer_2835 is the inverse capture operation. Its EGA buffer layout stores plane 0, 1, 2, and 3 bytes consecutively for every screen byte.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:29D5">V: DrawHorizontalVideoRun_29D5 writes one adapter-native run. CGA expands a 2-bit color across a byte, Tandy expands a 4-bit color, EGA uses write mode 2, and VGA writes the byte color directly.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2B00">V: CopyVideoRegion_2B00 copies an adapter-native rectangle between FAR video-layout buffers. EGA uses latch/write mode 1; CGA and Tandy follow their interleaved scanline banks; VGA is linear.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2DB0">V: FillVideoRectangle_2DB0 accepts an 8x8-tile rectangle, converts its height to scanlines and width to adapter bytes, packs the logical color for CGA/Tandy, and uses EGA write mode 2.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:2F05">V: Draw8x8VideoTile_2F05 consumes one adapter-native tile: 10h CGA bytes, 20h Tandy bytes, 20h EGA plane bytes, or 40h VGA bytes.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:32F4">V: LoadScreenAssetToWorkBuffer_32F4 loads and expands one indexed screen resource, then applies the non-VGA packed-pixel and CGA layout conversions.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="34D5:000C">V: CaptureVideoTileStrip_000C allocates and returns a far buffer containing tileCount consecutive 8x8 screen tiles, wrapping X after column 27h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6C12">V: 100h-byte Roland MPU-401 transmit ring with write/read/count words at 6D12h/6D14h/6D16h.</annotation>
