      <annotation addr="3A6A:6252">V: MIDITicksPerBeat_6252 is derived from FF 58 and converts the optional elapsed-tick counter into beats.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6254">V: MIDIBeatsPerMeasure_6254 is derived from FF 58 and converts elapsed beats into complete measures.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:625E">V: MIDIBeatTickRemainder_625E carries MIDI ticks toward the next complete beat.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6260">V: MIDIMeasureBeatRemainder_6260 carries beats toward the next complete measure.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6262">V: MIDIMeasureCount_6262 accumulates complete measures while playback flag 08h enables musical-time tracking.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6265">V: MIDIRunningStatus_6265 supplies the prior channel status when an event begins with a data byte.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6266">V: MIDIChannelEventDispatch_6266 contains seven near targets for status families 8xh through Exh inside ServiceMIDISequenceTick_01E8.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6274">V: MIDISystemEventDispatch_6274 contains sixteen near targets for statuses F0h through FFh inside ServiceMIDISequenceTick_01E8.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:6728">V: MIDIChannelMap_6728 is a 16-byte logical-to-physical channel map loaded from the engine-specific FF 01 event and reset to identity.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:4DFD">Read one 8-row EGA planar tile from video-memory segment A200h into a 32-byte far buffer. For each row, select Graphics Controller read-map planes 0 through 3 via ports 03CEh/03CFh and store the four plane bytes consecutively. sourceByteColumn plus sourceTileRow times 320 selects the first EGA byte; each following row advances by the 40-byte planar screen stride.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:4EAA">Read the color-display Input Status Register 1 at port 03DAh and return vertical-retrace bit 3. A nonzero result means vertical retrace is active.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:4EC2">Synchronize with a vertical-retrace edge through Input Status Register 1 at port 03DAh. Argument 1 first waits for retrace to be inactive and then waits for its leading edge; every other value first waits for retrace to begin and then returns at its trailing edge.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:7FEE">VerticalRetraceEdgeMode_7FEE: edge selected for display synchronization. Value 0 waits for the trailing/end edge; value 1 waits for the leading/start edge.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:0214">[V] Coordinate the complete campaign-to-tactical boundary. Derive the zero-based scenario ordinal from DS:254C[CampaignStageIndex_24D6] plus ScenarioVariantIndex_24D8; stage 08h cancels that addition and uses the base unchanged. Convert it to ASCII 1-9/A-T, load tactical audio, run 1A1F:0000, release battle resources, and restore campaign video, font, cursor, and music state.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:0387">[V] Switch video adapter mode at the tactical battle boundary, restore the common palette, optionally show the scenario result, and rebuild the screen, cursor, and captured title-strip resources in the new adapter representation.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:329E">[V] On VGA, copy the first 16 RGB palette triplets into DAC entries 00h, 10h, 20h through F0h and install the resulting 256-entry palette.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:5789">[V] Draw the successful or unsuccessful scenario-completion text according to CampaignFlags_24DF bit 0, then seed the completion-message timer at DS:5923 with 0Bh.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:2B11">[V] ScenarioCompletedText_2B11 is the NUL-terminated string "Scenario completed successfully" rendered by ShowScenarioCompletionStatus_5789.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:2B31">[V] ScenarioFailedText_2B31 is the NUL-terminated string "Scenario completed unsuccessfully" rendered by ShowScenarioCompletionStatus_5789.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:5923">[V] TacticalUpdateDelayTicks_5923 is decremented once per BIOS INT 1Ch tick. Tactical play reloads it from DS:17DA; the result banner reuses it with 0Bh ticks (about 0.604 seconds).</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:02B4">[V] Write '1' to MECHSETX.ICN character +07h. Preserve it for scenario suffixes below 'F' and for 'T'; otherwise overwrite it with '2'. Thus SCENE1-E/T use MECHSET1 and SCENEF-S use MECHSET2.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:03D4">[V] Add ASCII '0' to the icon-set argument, write the same selector to ICONSETx.ICN and DESTROYx.ICN character +07h, then load resource descriptors 3Eh, 3Dh, and ICONLIST.DAT descriptor 3Fh.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:0468">[V] resourcePath is followed by destinationPage at BP+0Ah. Advance DS:83E2 by destinationPage * 8000h bytes, decode into that icon page, and on EGA convert it to planar video segment A400h + destinationPage * 0200h.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:0517">[V] Not a procedure: MOV SP,BP / POP BP / RETF is the epilogue of LoadTacticalIconResource_0468. The tactical map loader begins at 051Bh.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:051B">[V] Convert the map number to filename character 1-9/A onward and write MAPx.MAP character +03h before opening descriptor 3Ch, reading its header, deriving dimensions and loading its terrain cells.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:0554">[V] Read the 0Ch-byte MAP header into DS:83EA; bytes 00h and 02h become MapWidth_00A6 and MapHeight_00A8.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:05E0">[V] PackedTerrainDamageRowBytes_00AA is ceil(MapWidth / 4), matching four two-bit damage states per byte.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="1A1F:05EC">[V] Read MapWidth * MapHeight terrain-type bytes over the header buffer at DS:83EA, then close the MAP resource.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="3A6A:254C">[V] ScenarioOrdinalBaseByCampaignStage_254C: 22 one-byte base ordinals indexed by CampaignStageIndex_24D6. InitializeTacticalScenario_0214 adjusts the selected value by ScenarioVariantIndex_24D8.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:324E">[V] For VGA, map the screen resource index through DS:1703, read exactly 300h palette bytes from that resource into DS:00AC, clear the active video buffer, and load the DAC palette. Other adapters only clear the buffer.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:4099">[V] Load a graphics resource into the supplied decode/display buffers. VGA uses the buffers directly; non-VGA swaps the load destination then converts it, and CGA additionally builds its transparency mask.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:4126">[V] Free the far buffer at DS:83EE, rebuild it from the four cursor geometry fields at DS:277B-2781, and store the replacement pointer back at DS:83EE.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0D73:4572">[V] Validate the opened save container: read the slot-table offset at file +02h, seek there, and accept version 0097h or later. On an older version, close the handle, show the invalid-version dialog, reopen the path, and retry.</annotation>
