      </procedure>
      <annotation addr="0800:0C87">V: NormalizeSegmentOffset_0C87 converts register pair DX:AX to an equivalent real-mode pointer whose offset is in 0000h..000Fh.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:3B9E">V: NormalizeFarPointer_3B9E normalizes a stack-supplied segment:offset pair and returns the equivalent pointer in DX:AX.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:542C">V: MultiplyUnsignedLong_542C returns the low 32 bits of unsigned DX:AX multiplied by CX:BX.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:5445">V: DivideUnsignedLong_5445 is the unsigned-quotient entry point of the Borland 32-bit division helper; adjacent internal entry points select signed or remainder modes.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:5507">V: ShiftRight32_DXAX_5507 logically shifts unsigned DX:AX right by CL and returns the result in DX:AX.</annotation>
      <annotation addr="0800:5526">V: CalculateFarPointerByteDistance_5526 subtracts the real-mode linear address CX:BX from DX:AX and returns the signed byte distance.</annotation>
